MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_001: Hyah! Hrrr-ah!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_002: Oho! Good technique there. You truly are Senghor's\ndaughter.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_003: Oh, it's Benditz... Uh, thanks?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_004: Feels pretty strange to receive praise from you.\nUsually you're more like...
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_005: "You call that technique? You call yourself a warrior?\nWell, do you?!"
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_006: Or my favorite, "That weapon isn't a toy—swing with\nconviction! Bah, kids today! Kids today!"
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_007: But look. Not only praise, but a smile to boot.\nWhat's gotten into you?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_008: I give praise when praise is due. Nothing strange\nabout that whatsoever.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_009: Hmm, is that right? Then why do I get the feeling\nthere's some ulterior motive here?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_010: Quiet, you! Now, let's get down to it. How about you\nquit the trading company and work for me?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_011: You want me...to work for you?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_012: Correct. I thought of it just now, seeing you train!\nSkill, youth, backbone... Very impressive.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_013: Plus, you've got a good head on your shoulders, and\nyou're General Senghor's daughter. The job is yours!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_014: And then, I'll be a lock for general. Yes, my position\nwill be guaranteed! Hah hah hah!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_015: Ah. So that's what this is...
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_016: Well? Do you want to study tactics under a great\ngeneral or not? I won't ask twice.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_017: I'll take you under my wing—my most trusted\ncompanion! You'd be a fool to refuse! Hah hah hah!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_018: Yeah, I'll have to decline anyway.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_019: What?! But why? I'm THE General Benditz!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_020: No, my father warned me about you. For starters,\nI know you're not even a REAL general.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_021: You're just a gossip who brags about having a title he\ndidn't earn. I'd never work for someone like that!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_022: Whaaat? Bah, kids today!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_023: Don't you come crawling back to me when you\nrealize you've made the mistake of a lifetime!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_C_024: Grrr! This pig-headed— You know what,\nnot my problem.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_001: Hmm... Now where is that infernal Ludia?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_002: She's really putting my better nature to the test...\nGiving her a second chance... Ah! There she is!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_003: Well, Ludia, hello! What are you reading there?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_004: Ugh...Benditz. This is The Great August's Art\nof War.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_005: WHAT?!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_006: Yeah, is that a problem? If you came here to throw\naround insults again, let's get to it already!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_007: Hahaha! You little genius! I should spread word\neverywhere about your sheer brilliance!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_008: Wait a second, are you being serious or did you just\nhit your head?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_009: I knew I saw something in you, girl! And now I've\ngot the evidence! That's my favorite book!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_010: Why, I just bought my fourth copy the other day.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_011: Fourth?!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_012: Exactly! So many weeks, so many merchants, but I\nfinally hunted down my latest extra copy.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_013: I haggled! I bartered! And in the end, I wrenched my\nprize from the shopkeep's hands.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_014: I'll admit, that's some insane passion. Going out of\nyour way to collect the same book is impressive.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_015: So, now you see the truth about me! I am a great\nman, it is true.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_016: Let me share with you MY copy of The Great\nAugust's Art of War...
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_017: My FIRST one, that is. It's worn out, tattered, the\ntitle illegible!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_018: I've always kept this book in my pocket—ever at\nhand the moment I need it.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_019: We've shared many battles together. I've fixed its\nrips and worn print many times. What do you think?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_020: Whoa! This is incredible. It's like holding history.\nWhat's all this handwriting in the margins?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_021: It's a first edition, you know. My first love, in a way.\nTo it, I've added my own notes and insights.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_022: With that book in hand, I dreamed my dream: I will\nbe a general as great as the Great August!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_023: I've jotted my every thought in there meticulously,\nbuilding upon its basic truths.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_024: I see... This must be why Benditz prioritizes the\nfundamentals in battle. I get it now...
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_025: Wow! You even have details on enemy movements.\nThis could be super useful... I-I want to read it!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_026: Well, if you insist... Delve into my 40 years of\nnotes all you like. Read at will.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_027: You're serious?
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_028: Well, Benditz, I didn't expect you had such a decent\nside, but I'm glad I was wrong.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_029: Aha! Well then, you're finally ready to join me!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_030: Again, the answer's no.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_031: What?! Refused twice? What insolence! This isn't\nover—not by a long shot!
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_032: He's a pain to be around, but he does have a pretty\nsteadfast resolve when he wants to.
MID_SE_Lou_Ven_B_033: I'm never working for him, though.